Title
Study of Use Case Diagram using UML
Aim

To understand and design a Use Case Diagram for a system using UML concepts.

Objective
To learn UML modeling
To identify actors and use cases
To represent interaction between user and system
Theory

A Use Case Diagram is a UML behavioral diagram used to represent the interaction between users (actors) and the system.

It describes:

Functional requirements of system
User interaction
System services

Use Case Diagram mainly focuses on:

“What the system does”
Components of Use Case Diagram
1. Actor

Represents user or external system.

Examples:

Student
Admin
Customer
2. Use Case

Represents system functionality.

Examples:

Login
Register
Upload File
3. System Boundary

Defines scope of system.

4. Association

Connection between actor and use case.

5. Include Relationship

Used when one use case always includes another use case.

6. Extend Relationship

Used for optional behavior.

Advantages
Easy to understand
Represents system functionality clearly
Helps in requirement analysis
Improves communication between developer and client
Applications
Banking System
Online Quiz System
Library Management
Hospital Management
